{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaQzV5gwMmeNqGMmqjL3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I proved `mySum_append` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` now finishes with no errors or warnings.\n\nThe proof works by induction on `xs`:\n\n```lean\ntheorem mySum_append (xs ys : List Nat) : mySum (xs ++ ys) = mySum xs + mySum ys := by\n  induction xs with\n  | nil => simp [mySum]\n  | cons x xs ih => simp [mySum, ih, Nat.add_assoc]\n```\n\n- **Empty list:** `[] ++ ys` simplifies to `ys`, and `mySum []` is `0`, so both sides are equal.\n- **Non-empty list (`x :: xs`):** expanding `mySum` gives `x + mySum (xs ++ ys)` on the left. The induction hypothesis rewrites that to `x + (mySum xs + mySum ys)`. Re-grouping the addition (`Nat.add_assoc`) then matches the right side, `(x + mySum xs) + mySum ys`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":8315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":338,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d2e238c-5872-470a-9fc4-9a830ed62c44","uuid":"42a87e28-592f-472b-bdf3-efeec0bbff72","timestamp":"2026-10-31T13:44:08.945Z","request_id":"req_011CgaQzUsXeq57Rj5XfUa53"}
